# drivers/TegraGM20B on the host:
#   gm20b_comp_test          TegraGM20BComp.h against nvgpu's gm20b: the compbit backing store's size, lines and base for
#                            every plausible CBC_PARAM, which page lists and binds may compress, a compressed bind's PTEs
#   gm20b_zcull_test         TegraGM20BZcull.h against nvgpu's zcull report for the X1's GR; its record is
#                            drm_nouveau_get_zcull_info's
#   gm20b_tiled_cache_test   TegraGM20BTiledCache.h: the tile coalescer's table in the golden context is deko3d's masked
#                            writes folded over sw_ctx's zero
#   gm20b_coherency_test     TegraGM20BCoherency.cpp: which IOSurface lock/unlock traps clean or invalidate an import,
#                            across imports of one surface and their release, and traps racing a release; each surface's
#                            layout decision (TegraGM20BTiled.cpp) and its contents tiled in place; CPU locks of a
#                            block-linear surface (TegraGM20BViews.cpp): rows in a scratch at the task's own address
#                            while the pages keep texels, shared readers, nested locks, writes put back, dead tasks
#   gm20b_fences_test        TegraGM20BExecSurfaces.cpp and TegraGM20BFences.h with the registry's writer records over a
#                            model of gpu_*.c's channels: which listed surfaces' writers an Exec waits for on the GPU (another
#                            channel's, unfinished, not killed), which imports it counts as written, and no list or the
#                            all-imports flag as before
#   gm20b_relayout_test      TegraGM20BRelayout.h's copy-engine pushes over a model of MAXWELL_DMA_COPY_A: every move
#                            gives back exactly TegraGM20BLayout.h's bytes, for every texel size and NIL's shapes
#   gm20b_copy_test          TegraGM20BCopyPush.h (TegraVIC's plane bounce) over the same model: rows at the new pitch
#                            from pitch, block-linear and two-plane sources; writer and syncpoint waits first, the
#                            syncpoint increment after the copy is in DRAM
#   gm20b_wiring_test        TegraGM20BSharedWiring.cpp: one wiring per task and range, shared while the task still
#                            maps it there, a racing publish, the last import's release
#   gm20b_tlb_test           TegraGM20BTlb.h over a GMMU model (PTEs, the L2's copies, a TLB per space, running work
#                            that refills it): GPU-ordered maps and synchronous unmaps never reach a released page
#   gm20b_pool_policy_test   TegraGM20BPoolPolicy.h (where a coherent BO's memory comes from) over a model of the pool
#                            when Maps opened: its first buffers come from system memory instead of being refused;
#                            MapKit's 4 KiB, the compositor's 16 MiB block, the floor, room for everyone
#   gm20b_prefault_test      TegraGM20BSurfacePrefault.h over a mock create ABI: which IOSurfaceRootUserClient outputs
#                            name a new surface, and which surfaces are faulted in (size, memory pressure)
#   gm20b_push_scan_test     TegraGM20BPushScan.h (the kernel's method-stream reader and the push profile's classes) over
#                            streams laid out as NVK and the raw path write them: every counter, each drawn target's
#                            image under its sample grid, a raw job's indirect command buffer draws inside their executed
#                            range (its macro slots the generator's), and no profile stamp after a push whose method
#                            continues, one the kernel could not read or one with an opcode NVK never writes
#   gm20b_target_peaks_test  SwitchGpuTargetPeaks.h: each process's largest target image since boot, and its line
#   gm20b_span_notes_test    SwitchGpuSpanNotes.h: the render server's long spans and the compositor's longest job
#   gm20b_preempt_landing_test SwitchGpuPreemptLanding.h: where a kick's preempt landed (a band's release, a job's end)
#   gm20b_compositor_sync_test SwitchGpuCompositorSync.h: the compositor's sync pushes, kicks behind an app apart
#   gm20b_cost_hist_test     TegraGM20BCostHist.h: the debug lines' buckets, and a p95 a single slow frame leaves alone
#   gm20b_sched_test         TegraGM20BSchedPolicy.h and tgm_hang_blame over deploy-2045's hang registers: what a
#                            compositor kick preempts, the interleaved runlist (full, empty, one level), which channel a
#                            late wait kills (the context GR cannot switch, a self-hung channel, never slow work)
#   gm20b_recover_test       TegraGM20BRecover.h over device boots 7 and 9: every SCHED_ERROR and BIND_ERROR code's name,
#                            which engine whose switch timed out is waited for, killed off or reset (a killed channel's
#                            context), which engines hold a channel at its unbind, that a PBDMA ENG_RESET or ACQUIRE never
#                            reaches nvkm as the channel's error; F-v1's twod_clear save timeout and its engine line
#   gm20b_kernel_hang_model_test  T-v5a's pool-scrub panic over a model of runlist 0 under hundreds of client
#                            kills: the rule before ends in it, the kernel channel's steps (TegraGM20BKernelHang.h)
#                            never do while a reset frees the GPU, and panic only once a clean reset of every engine
#                            did not
#   gm20b_eng_reset_order_test  recover_engine.c's hold of the PBDMA's ENG_RESET over a model of an engine reset and
#                            the interrupt pass: at every point the pass can run, the PBDMA goes on only once the engine is
#                            back, its live channel preempted, a killed one's method dropped
#   gm20b_view_merge_test    TegraGM20BViewMerge.h: a CPU write lock's unlock keeps the bytes a GPU write left where the
#                            CPU wrote none, byte by byte
#   gm20b_acquire_test       TegraGM20BAcquire.h: the RAMFC ACQUIRE word as nvgpu computes it, CCSR's parked states, the
